DOMAIN_OVERVIEW:
This domain covers Dussel's location within the modernity/coloniality/
decoloniality (MCD) network alongside Quijano, Mignolo, Maldonado-Torres,
Escobar, Grosfoguel, and Castro-Gomez. Core shared concepts include
coloniality of power (Quijano), geopolitics of knowledge and border
thinking (Mignolo), transmodernity (Dussel), pluriversalism (Grosfoguel,
Mignolo), and the decolonial turn (Maldonado-Torres). The network
converges on rejecting the Eurocentric narrative of modernity as an
intra-European achievement and on positing 1492 as modernity's
inception, but divides on the relative weight of political economy
(Quijano, Grosfoguel) versus epistemic/semiotic critique (Mignolo) and
on Dussel's analectical/liberation-theological framing.

RELEVANCE_TO_PROJECT:
Situating Dussel's Eurocentrism critique requires showing both his
contribution to the MCD network's shared diagnosis and the points where
his philosophy of liberation diverges from Quijano's structural sociology
and Mignolo's semiotic decolonial option. Maldonado-Torres's framing of
Dussel within the decolonial turn is essential reception literature.

NOTABLE_GAPS:
Few sources treat internal disagreements within the MCD network with
analytic precision; most are exegetical or applied. Critical engagements
(Hull; Geneciran; Lindner) are valuable counterpoints.

SYNTHESIS_GUIDANCE:
Use Pimenta and Maldonado-Torres for Dussel's intellectual trajectory
within the network; use Grosfoguel and Mignolo for the shared
transmodern/border-thinking vocabulary; use Hull, Geneciran, and Lindner
for principled critique.

KEY_POSITIONS:
- MCD network insiders (Mignolo, Grosfoguel, Maldonado-Torres, Escobar):
  7 papers - elaborate and apply shared concepts
- Critical/external readings (Hull, Geneciran, Lindner, Harding): 4 papers
  - challenge or reframe decolonial theory
- Dussel-network synthesis (Pimenta, Misoczky, Velez/Tuana): 3 papers
  - locate Dussel specifically within the network
====================================================================
}

